Not worse in my opinion. Not on the native "best" resolution of the game itself. If the game's best resolution is 1080p, and you run DLSS, you'll get the benefits of the best anti aliasing, the best render quality you can get, and even better frame rates than AA off. If you ran the same game at 4k, you'll get DLSS AA, decent image quality, and the frame rates of 1080p.
New games are upon us that supports RT and DLSS, and people will see for themselves the significant differences those new technologies can bring.

